<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "FabricRouting">
<!ENTITY author "RifleJock">
<!--
  Versioning — Unraid plugin updates use strcmp() (lexicographic), NOT version_compare.
  No hyphens. Bump only this entity; asset ?v= uses it.

  Rules (ibigsnet fleet — StorageGuard / Thunderbolt Net / FabricRouting / NBD Export):
    YYYY.MM.DD       first release that calendar day
    YYYY.MM.DDaa     2nd same day, then ab, ac, ... az, ba, bb, ...
  Two-letter only after the bare date — never single a–z
  (strcmp treats "aa" as older than "z").
  Calendar day = lab wall clock (not invented “tomorrow”). See RELEASES.md.

  UI: Network Settings siblings via ibigsGotoNetTab(Title) — never deep-link
  /Settings/ThunderboltNet or /Settings/FabricRouting (standalone CA pages).
-->
<!ENTITY version "2026.08.14am">
<!ENTITY launch "Settings/FabricRouting">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ibigsnet/FabricRouting/main/fabricrouting.plg">
<!ENTITY github "ibigsnet/FabricRouting">
<!ENTITY raw "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ibigsnet/FabricRouting/main">
<!ENTITY plugdir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting">
<!ENTITY configdir "/boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
  author="&author;"
  version="&version;"
  launch="&launch;"
  pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
  icon="project-diagram"
  min="6.12.0"
  support="https://github.com/&github;/issues"
  project="https://github.com/&github;"
  readme="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/stable/README.md">

<CHANGES>
###&version;
- Lead copy: short product blurb; move when-to-use / Thunderbolt split into <strong>What is FRR?</strong>
  (drop “not Routing Table” banner and Need this strip).

###2026.08.14al
- UI: blue <code>inline_help</code> on Advanced core daemons (zebra / fabricd / staticd), optional
  protocols, install-on-start, catalog URL, and start-on-Apply.

###2026.08.14ak
- **Fix:** package job no longer hangs on Step 4/4 — close stdio / hard-timeout frrinit so
  openBox reaches DONE; skip start when zebra already running (packages were already OK).

###2026.08.14aj
- **Package UX v2:** radio pick (Latest / Previous / Flash) + **Download &amp; Install packages**
  via Unraid `openBox` (Nvidia-style log + DONE — do not close early). Settings Apply no longer
  downloads packages. Collapse Advanced daemons. Timeout on `frrinit.sh` start so WebUI cannot hang.

###2026.08.14ai
- Network Settings tab order: `Menu=NetworkSettings:z` so Fabric Routing sorts **after** stock
  Routing Table (far right). Numeric ranks (`:1200`) sort *before* unranked stock tabs with
  SORT_NATURAL — that left FR stuck next to Thunderbolt/tbn. UI copy: packages-only vs TBN policy.

###2026.08.14ah
- Attempted tab pin at `:1200` (still before Interface Extra / Routing Table under SORT_NATURAL).

###2026.08.14ag
- Wording: spell out **Thunderbolt** (not ambiguous “TB”, which can mean terabyte).
- **Rename:** product id **FabricRouting** (public **Fabric Routing**). No “Unraid” in the product name (trademark). Legacy UnraidFRR paths migrated on install.
- Install URL: `fabricrouting.plg` on `ibigsnet/FabricRouting`.

###2026.08.14ab
- **Lab channel:** On branch `main`, PluginURL + raw FILE sources point at `main` (lab uninstall/reinstall testing).
- Branch `stable` remains the CA/production pin (see RELEASE-CHANNEL.md). Ship by merging to stable and rewriting entities to stable.

###2026.08.14aa
- **License:** GNU GPLv3 or later (copyright ibigs, LLC; Author: RifleJock).
- **Release channel:** PluginURL, raw FILE sources, and package catalog pin to branch `stable`.
- SECURITY.md: idle install, no eth0/br0, packages only on Apply, uninstall scope.

###2026.08.13ab
- Docs: public sanitization — SUPPORTED matrix and lab notes use **Machine A/B** patterns (no personal hostnames/IPs); [lab-two-node-fabric.md](docs/lab-two-node-fabric.md).

###2026.08.13aa
- Fleet standard: companion links use **`ibigsGotoNetTab`** (aliases `frrGotoNetTab` / …); apply-on-load for `ibigsWantTab`; never deep-link standalone CA paths.
- Docs: RELEASES cross-plugin UI link table.

###2026.08.13
- UI: companion “Network Settings → Thunderbolt” under strip, not `/Settings/ThunderboltNet`.
- Versioning: bare `2026.08.13` after historical single-letter 12a–g.

###2026.08.12g
- Docs: first-time-setup.md — need/skip, settings guide, first Apply checklist; linked from DOCS + UI.
- UI: companion link (buggy) pointed at /Settings/ThunderboltNet; fixed in 2026.08.13.
- Defaults: Auto-download **No** (opt-in network fetch); first-time Yes → Apply still works.
- UI: beginner “What is FRR?” section; clearer package/daemon help; no public Nvidia branding.
- Docs: defaults-rationale.md; sanitize Nvidia comparisons in public docs.
- **Boot / plg install is files-only** — no package download, no frr_apply (sync or background). Unraid re-runs every .plg at boot; heavy work there could block rc.local → emhttp → array.
- **Network download only on Settings → Fabric Routing → Apply** (auto_download). Network package fetch only on Settings → Apply (flash cache + rehydrate on array start).
- **Array start** rehydrates packages **already on flash** into RAM (`frr_rehydrate_local` / local_only); never fetches catalog. Detached via `at`/`nohup` so emhttp events stay non-blocking.
- Docs: boot-lifecycle.md; install-uninstall-audit + automation-design aligned with Unraid plugin best practice.
- Versioning comment aligned with StorageGuard / Thunderbolt Net (two-letter suffixes only).

###2026.08.12d
- Apply: progress-frame messages (do not close — same UX as other Unraid Settings progress dialogs); single-flight lock.
- Catalog: do not keep empty-bundle cache for a full hour (fixes stale “No match yet”).
- Status: flash package names; no-match help + SUPPORTED link; fix plugin version detection path.
- Docs: SUPPORTED matrix — lab-confirmed vs suggested-compatible Unraid versions.
- Docs: frr-and-unraid-routing.md — stock Routing Table vs FRR; what Unraid can/cannot leverage.
- Docs: scope-and-safety + DOCS cross-links for routing-table impact.
- Uninstall: stop via /usr/sbin/frrinit.sh; kill mgmtd; always removepkg-sweep frr-* and libyang-*.
- Docs: packages/SUPPORTED.md — Unraid product version matrix (lab-proven 7.3.x x86_64).
- Docs: product-roadmap.md — interfaces/metrics UI, CA/forum, ambitions (Proxmox, multi-node AI).
- First FRR package set: libyang 2.1.148 + frr 10.7.0 (fabricd) for Unraid 7.x x86_64 — GitHub Release pkg-10.7.0 + manifest catalog.
- frr_try_start: prefer /usr/sbin/frrinit.sh (our packages).
- Docs: two-host lab fabric pattern; package build plan; packages/build scripts.
- Docs: Contents/TOC on DOCS.md.
- UI: collapsible About; tighter companion strip (less wall of text).
- UI: sectioned Status / Packages / Core daemons / Optional protocols (NBD-style density); less wall of text.
- Public name: **Fabric Routing** (Network Settings tab) · **Fabric Routing (FRR)** (CA / Plugins blurb). Plugin id FabricRouting.
- Note: single-letter 12d was non-standard; use two-letter suffixes going forward.

###2026.08.11ag
- Network Settings tab **Fabric Routing** (with Routing Table / Interface Rules), not System Settings tile.
- Title explains FRR packages vs stock Routing Table; plugin id stays FabricRouting.

###2026.08.11af
- Fix Settings placement: **System Settings tile** (`Menu="OtherSettings"`), not embedded section on /Settings (`Settings:50` was wrong).
- Uninstall: also remove any stray FabricRouting/FRR .page copies under webGui/dynamix; clear /tmp plugin remnants.

###2026.08.11ae
- Docs/UI: when to install (rings, multi-hop, Proxmox+Unraid) vs skip (single static Thunderbolt cable); roles vs Thunderbolt Net OpenFabric policy.

###2026.08.11ad
- UI: status labels distinguish plugin version / Unraid product / FRR package set; USB4STREAM is kernel (not Unraid 7.2 product); companion strip wording.
- Catalog matching uses Unraid product version + arch only (not uname -r).

###2026.08.11ac
- Docs: DOCS/RELEASES/docs index aligned with Storage Guard + Thunderbolt Net (CA + raw install, uninstall).
- Uninstall: stop FRR, removepkg managed packages, clear emhttp + flash config — no leftover hooks; does not touch network.cfg or Thunderbolt Net.
- Install finish message: automated Apply path (no manual package drop).

###2026.08.11ab
- Package catalog: manifest + sha256 + installpkg + array-start rehydrate from flash.
- UI: package channel, auto-download default Yes; status shows Unraid version/arch/bundle match.
- Docs: automation-design.md; DOCS/README updated for full control by the plugin.

###2026.08.11aa
- README: short Unraid Plugins-list blurb (same format as Storage Guard / Thunderbolt Net); long docs stay in DOCS.md.

###2026.08.11
- Initial public release: standalone FRR package install hooks, daemon toggles (zebra/fabricd default on), Settings → FRR UI, array-start install, companion marker for Thunderbolt Net.
- Docs: detailed what-it-does guide, scope/safety (host-wide routing, not Thunderbolt-only), LAN-safe defaults, Thunderbolt Net integration.
- Idle and safe when packages/ is empty. Does not require Thunderbolt Net. CA listing via ibigsnet/unraid-templates.
</CHANGES>

<!--
  FabricRouting is intentionally separate from ThunderboltNet:
  package install is invasive; users opt in. No PHP requires across plugins.
  Removal must not leave broken Unraid UI (StorageGuard/ThunderboltNet discipline).
-->

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
echo "FabricRouting: preparing directories..."
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fabricrouting
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/include
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/event
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/packages
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/packages

# Migrate legacy UnraidFRR flash state (pre-rename) into FabricRouting
if [ -d /boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR ] && [ ! -f /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/FabricRouting.cfg ]; then
  echo "FabricRouting: migrating config from legacy UnraidFRR..."
  mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting
  if [ -f /boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR/UnraidFRR.cfg ]; then
    cp -a /boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR/UnraidFRR.cfg /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/FabricRouting.cfg
  fi
  if [ -d /boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR/packages ]; then
    mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/packages
    cp -a /boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR/packages/. /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/packages/ 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  for f in companion.json manifest.cache.json unraidfrr.log fabricrouting.log; do
    [ -f "/boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR/$f" ] && cp -a "/boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR/$f" "/boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/" 2>/dev/null || true
  done
fi
# Remove legacy emhttp tree so old Settings id does not linger
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/UnraidFRR /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraidfrr
rm -f /var/log/plugins/unraidfrr.plg /boot/config/plugins/unraidfrr.plg 2>/dev/null || true
# Never block a new install on a stale Apply lock from a killed session
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/apply.lock
echo "FabricRouting: directories ready."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/FabricRouting.page">
<URL>&raw;/FabricRouting.page?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/default.cfg">
<URL>&raw;/default.cfg?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/README.md">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
**Fabric Routing (FRR)**

Optional FRRouting for Unraid. Boot only loads the plugin UI. Use **Download &amp; Install packages** under Network Settings → Fabric Routing (openBox log + DONE). Array start rehydrates from flash. Standalone: Thunderbolt Net not required. Does not edit eth0/br0 by default.
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/packages/manifest.json">
<URL>&raw;/packages/manifest.json?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/include/frr-lib.php">
<URL>&raw;/include/frr-lib.php?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/include/frr-update.php">
<URL>&raw;/include/frr-update.php?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-install-packages">
<URL>&raw;/scripts/frr-install-packages?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-apply">
<URL>&raw;/scripts/frr-apply?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-download">
<URL>&raw;/scripts/frr-download?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-packages-job">
<URL>&raw;/scripts/frr-packages-job?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-force-cleanup">
<URL>&raw;/scripts/frr-force-cleanup?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/event/started">
<URL>&raw;/event/started?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
echo "FabricRouting: finishing install (files only — no package download)..."
chmod 755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-install-packages 2>/dev/null || true
chmod 755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-apply 2>/dev/null || true
chmod 755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-download 2>/dev/null || true
chmod 755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-packages-job 2>/dev/null || true
chmod 755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/scripts/frr-force-cleanup 2>/dev/null || true
chmod 755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/event/started 2>/dev/null || true
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/packages
# Stale Apply lock must not block a later package job
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/apply.lock
if [ ! -f /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/FabricRouting.cfg ]; then
  if [ -f /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/default.cfg ]; then
    cp -a /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/default.cfg /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/FabricRouting.cfg
    echo "FabricRouting: created default FabricRouting.cfg"
  fi
fi
# Companion marker only. NEVER frr_apply / download here.
# Unraid re-runs this plg every boot (rc.local); network package work belongs on
# Settings → Download & Install packages. Array start rehydrates flash (event/started).
php -r 'require_once "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting/include/frr-lib.php"; frr_write_companion_marker();' 2>/dev/null || true
echo "FabricRouting: install complete (plugin files registered)."
echo "FabricRouting: Download packages: Settings → Network Settings → Fabric Routing → Download & Install packages."
echo "FabricRouting: Leave the openBox window open until DONE. Hard-refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R)."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
echo "FabricRouting: removing plugin (full cleanup)..."

# Legacy product id (pre-rename)
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/UnraidFRR /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraidfrr
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/UnraidFRR
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/unraidfrr.plg /var/log/plugins/unraidfrr.plg 2>/dev/null || true

# 0) Stop any in-flight Apply / background install
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/apply.lock
pkill -f 'frr_apply|FabricRouting/include/frr-lib' 2>/dev/null || true

# 1) Stop FRR so package removal is not blocked and daemons do not linger
systemctl stop frr 2>/dev/null || true
/usr/sbin/frrinit.sh stop 2>/dev/null || true
/usr/lib/frr/frrinit.sh stop 2>/dev/null || true
service frr stop 2>/dev/null || true
for p in zebra fabricd bgpd ospfd ospf6d isisd staticd bfdd watchfrr mgmtd; do
  pkill -x "$p" 2>/dev/null || true
done
sleep 1
for p in zebra fabricd bgpd ospfd ospf6d isisd staticd bfdd watchfrr mgmtd; do
  pkill -9 -x "$p" 2>/dev/null || true
done

# 2) removepkg — MANIFEST first, then glob any leftover frr/libyang we may have installed
MAN=/boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting/packages/MANIFEST.txt
if [ -f "$MAN" ]; then
  while IFS= read -r line || [ -n "$line" ]; do
    line="${line%%#*}"
    line="$(echo "$line" | tr -d '\r' | xargs)"
    [ -z "$line" ] && continue
    base="$(basename "$line")"
    pkgname="$(echo "$base" | sed -E 's/\.(t[gx]z|tar\.gz)$//')"
    if command -v removepkg >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      echo "FabricRouting: removepkg $pkgname"
      removepkg "$pkgname" 2>/dev/null || removepkg "$base" 2>/dev/null || true
    fi
  done < "$MAN"
fi
if command -v removepkg >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  for pkgpath in /var/log/packages/frr-* /var/log/packages/libyang-*; do
    [ -e "$pkgpath" ] || continue
    pkgname="$(basename "$pkgpath")"
    echo "FabricRouting: removepkg sweep $pkgname"
    removepkg "$pkgname" 2>/dev/null || true
  done
fi

# 3) Runtime state left by FRR packages
rm -rf /var/run/frr /run/frr 2>/dev/null || true
# Keep /etc/frr and /var/lib/frr? Clean removal = wipe runtime config we created
rm -rf /etc/frr /var/lib/frr 2>/dev/null || true
rm -f /var/log/fabricrouting.log 2>/dev/null || true

# 4) Remove emhttp plugin tree (case variants — avoid leftover Settings pages)
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/fabricrouting
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/Unraidfrr

find /usr/local/emhttp/webGui /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/dynamix -maxdepth 1 -type f \
  \( -name 'FabricRouting.page' -o -name 'FabricRouting-*.page' -o -name 'fabricrouting.page' \) \
  -delete 2>/dev/null || true

# 5) Flash state (cfg, package cache, marker, locks)
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/fabricrouting
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/Unraidfrr

# 6) Temp + log plugins remnants
rm -f /tmp/plugins/fabricrouting.plg /tmp/plugins/fabricrouting.txt 2>/dev/null || true
rm -f /tmp/plugins/FabricRouting* /tmp/inline*-fabricrouting.sh 2>/dev/null || true
rm -f /var/log/plugins/fabricrouting.plg /var/log/plugins/FabricRouting.plg 2>/dev/null || true

# 7) Sanity
FAIL=0
if which vtysh >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo "FabricRouting: WARNING — vtysh still on PATH (foreign FRR install?)"
  FAIL=1
fi
if ls /var/log/packages/frr-* /var/log/packages/libyang-* >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo "FabricRouting: WARNING — package records still present under /var/log/packages"
  FAIL=1
fi
if [ -e /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/FabricRouting ] || [ -e /boot/config/plugins/FabricRouting ]; then
  echo "FabricRouting: WARNING — plugin paths still present"
  FAIL=1
fi
if pgrep -x zebra >/dev/null 2>&1 || pgrep -x fabricd >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo "FabricRouting: WARNING — FRR processes still running"
  FAIL=1
fi
if [ "$FAIL" = "0" ]; then
  echo "FabricRouting: cleanup verified clean."
fi

echo "FabricRouting: removed."
echo "FabricRouting: did not modify network.cfg, br0, Docker, or Thunderbolt Net."
echo "FabricRouting: hard-refresh the browser (Ctrl+Shift+R)."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
